(This post contains spoilers!)

SLASH'EM is about more monsters, more objects and more strategies.

If you are frustrated with SLASH'EM, then think more. If you believe
that the game is broken because roles do not play like they do in
vanilla, then think more. The game feels frustrating or unbalanced to
you because you have not explored the different strategies needed for
SLASH'EM, because you do not appreciate how roleplaying in SLASH'EM is
different from roleplaying in vanilla.

I play chaotic elves, so my vanilla heroes are always Priests, Rangers
or Wizards, while my SLASH'EM heroes are droven Priests, Wizards, or
any of several other roles. The drow can sometimes put a sleep spell on
their enemies by meleeing them bare-handed; in this case SLASH'EM is
easier than NetHack.

My most successful SLASH'EM character was a Barbarian, that
Cleaver-wielding fighter. I died in the Neutral Quest (one of the three
quests for alignment keys). SLASH'EM has many side levels, and I have
not yet a good strategy for when to play them.

I have played Fire Mages and Ice Mages. How is a Fire Mage different
from a Wizard? A Wizard might not start with an attack spell (like the
force bolt of vanilla Wizards). A Fire Mage starts with intrinsic fire
resistance, wand of fire, and a spell that summons a flaming sphere. I
have not really learned to exploit them well. My last Fire Mage made
the mistake of wearing metal armor including a mithril-coat and
avoiding the spells. I need to try to play a Fire Mage like a Fire
Mage.

The Necromancer and the Undead Slayer, I had some practice with. These
roles are difficult until you think about how to play them differently
from other roles. Both roles have intrinsic sickness resistance and can
eat old corpses; they should think differently about corpses. With my
next Necromancer or Undead Slayer, I want to give more attention to the
#technique command. I think that my ignorance of these roles'
techniques harmed my play much.

Blessed is variety! I believe that my experience in both NetHack and
SLASH'EM will make sooner that day when I achieve my first ascension in
either game.

SLASH'EM is a great game. Go get 0.0.7E7F2 from http://www.slashem.org
or try http://slashem.crash-override.net for an NAO-like server.

